# Webview (Last 100)

- Table columns: TIME, MODEL, COST, TOKENS, INPUT / OUTPUT, KIND. Newest first. Monospace body.
- Four tabs: **Last N Cursor queries** (default 1000), **Statistics**, **Charts**, **Settings**. Style with `--vscode-*` variables only. Tabs, buttons, inputs, and chips are ghost/pill controls: theme-mixed borders and top-shine gradients, not `--vscode-button-background`. Dark and light both derive from the IDE tokens (`body.vscode-dark` / `body.vscode-light`). User-chosen status colors come from settings (`okColor` / `warnColor`), not a hardcoded marketplace palette in CSS. Packaged defaults are mint/coral on dark themes and darker green/red on light themes.
- CSP nonce; `default-src 'none'`. No inline handlers without nonce.
- Host → webview: `{ type: 'data', events, spikeTokenThreshold, showSpikeWarning, showCriticalAlert, criticalTokenThreshold, criticalCostUsdThreshold, okColor, warnColor, historyLimit, pollIntervalMinutes, showStatusBar, showToday, minimalMode, recentQueryCount, statusBarPreview, stats, charts, periods, mtd, refreshing }`. Webview → host: `{ type: 'ready' }` | `{ type: 'close' }` | `{ type: 'refresh' }` | `{ type: 'setSpikeThreshold', value }` | `{ type: 'setShowSpikeWarning', value }` | `{ type: 'setShowCriticalAlert', value }` | `{ type: 'setCriticalTokenThreshold', value }` | `{ type: 'setCriticalCostUsdThreshold', value }` | `{ type: 'setShowStatusBar', value }` | `{ type: 'setShowToday', value }` | `{ type: 'setMinimalMode', value }` | `{ type: 'setRecentQueryCount', value }` | `{ type: 'setPollIntervalMinutes', value }` | `{ type: 'setOkColor', value }` | `{ type: 'setWarnColor', value }` | `{ type: 'setHistoryLimit', value }`. Apply Warn at immediately (input debounce + Apply). Show last (100–10,000, default 1000), Auto-refresh (1–60 min), and Critical alert token/dollar thresholds apply on Apply / Enter / blur — not while typing, because `min=100` on Show last rejects partial values like `2` when typing `2000`, and Critical alert `10000` k would otherwise save as `1` / `10` / `100`. Queries toolbar has **Refresh** (postMessage), **Over limit only** (client-side filter to token-spike `!` rows; off and disabled when Show warnings is off), plus Export CSV. Export CSV and Open Dashboard are allowlisted `command:` links (`cursorCost.exportCsv`, `cursorCost.openDashboard`).
- Settings tab holds every `cursorCost.*` key. Status-bar settings live in one fieldset (sample preview, Show status bar, content, warnings, colors) with section titles inside the card. Together they include show status bar, Show Today, Minimal mode, and recent status-bar queries (1–10, default 3). The preview uses example spend, not live totals. **Critical alert** is a separate fieldset (blocking dialog at 10M tokens or $5 by default; independent of Show warnings). Recent queries: Show last. Refresh: Auto-refresh interval. When Show warnings is off: no `!` and no green/red on the bar or table. Select/`option` lists use `--vscode-dropdown-*` (not input foreground alone) so dark themes stay readable.
- Statistics tab: Current/Today with progress meters, **Monthly cost forecast** (plan-dependent: Team/Business/Enterprise → dollars + one Spend series; Pro → included % for Cursor Models / Other Models. Team: this month’s spend vs working days so far × daily budget. Pro: one meter per quota with cycle % + run-out date; 0–100% chart with used + forecast + ideal per quota; range toggle Today / 7 days / Month, default Month; forecast in warm dashed colors, ideal in cool dotted blues), cycle facts, Last N sample (total, average, median, cache hit, cost per 1M tokens, token mix, highlights), spend-by-model/kind bars.
- Charts tab: two SVG series (tokens over time, cost over time) plus the same **Monthly cost forecast** control as Statistics (meters, Today / 7 days / Month range, used/forecast/ideal). Oldest → newest; per-query bars + cumulative line. Hover tip is a compact card: title, subtitle, label/value rows (not a pre-wrap dump). Below: three cards (Today / This month / All time) with cost, cache hit, and input/output/cache mix. `charts` is `{ timestamp, time, model, tokens, costUsd }[]`. `mtd` is `{ title, value, body, bars, metrics, overPace, verdict, unit, max, chart, forecast, series }` where `title` is `Monthly cost forecast`, `value` is unused (empty), `verdict` is `ok` | `tight` | `over`, `unit` is `usd` | `percent`, `max` caps the forecast axis (`100` for percent, `null` scales to data), `chart` is `{ date, weekday, workingDayIndex, dayUsedUsd, usedUsd, allowanceUsd }[]` (1st → today), `forecast` is the day backbone `{ date, weekday, workingDayIndex, allowanceUsd }[]` (1st → last day) and `series` is `{ id, label, day, used, forecast, ideal, runOutDate, runOutLabel }[]` — one line per included quota (Cursor Models, Other Models) or a single `Spend` line on dollar plans. `day`/`used` are null after today, `forecast` spans the whole month, `ideal` is leftover ceiling from today to month end (`null` before today), `runOutDate` is the first day the forecast hits the ceiling (or null if it lasts), and values are dollars or included % when `unit` is `percent`. `periods` is the three cards. No cookies or access tokens.
- Payload must not include cookies, access tokens, or emails beyond what PRD shows in the table.
- Keep JS small (vanilla). Do not add React.
